00:01:55,714 --> 00:02:01,714
The Cowboy and the Frenchman is a comedy, western film directed by David Lynch.

2
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:57,428
A grizzled, hard-of-hearing cowboy, Slim, and his two friends, Dusty
and Pete, capture a mysterious, well-dressed Frenchman.

3
00:05:47,142 --> 00:05:53,142
Slim, played by Harry Dean Stanton.

4
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:48,857
Pierre the Frenchman, played by Frederic Golchan.

5
00:09:38,571 --> 00:09:44,571
Dusty, played by Tracey Walter.

6
00:11:34,285 --> 00:11:40,285
Pete, played by Jack Nance.

7
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Broken Feather, played by Michael Horse.

8
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Howdy, played by Rick Guillory.

9
00:17:21,428 --> 00:17:27,428
The Short Films of David Lynch (2002) is a DVD collection of the early student
and commissioned film work of American filmmaker David Lynch.

10
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:23,142
As such, the collection does not include Lynch's later short
works, which are listed in the filmography.

11
00:21:12,857 --> 00:21:18,857
The DVD contains introductions by Lynch to each film.

12
00:23:08,571 --> 00:23:14,571
The film explores themes of surreal, surrealism, short film.

13
00:25:04,285 --> 00:25:10,285
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
